  "body": "The equal-steps depth ladder of #2012 is a field of the operation's `links.approach` object. Four depth-stepping operations have no `links` object. They cannot save the parameter.\n\nThe operations:\n\n- Face (staged facing with Top Z and a stepdown)\n- Trace\n- Engrave\n- Trochoidal Slot\n\nWhat happens:\n\n- These operations always use the remainder ladder. The last step keeps the remainder.\n- The other depth-stepping milling operations have the `equal_steps` parameter (#2012).\n\nWhat to do:\n\n- Give each of the four operations a saved `equal_steps` parameter. The default is off.\n- Send the stepdown through `camcraft_motion::machining2d::equal_stepdown` when the parameter is on. The level law does not change.\n- Make the parameter undoable through `EditOperationParams`.\n- Make sure that the MCP `edit_operation` patch reaches the parameter.\n- Add a row to the page of each operation.\n\nNotes:\n\n- This changes posted G-code only when the parameter is on (safety floor: `effort:high`).\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/2012-equal-steps.md`.\n- Turning operations have their own infeed laws. They are not part of this issue.\n\nDone means:\n\n- Each of the four operations has the parameter, with undo, a project file key and an MCP field.\n- A test pins the levels of the two modes for each of the four operations.\n",
